---
import './Trust.css';
---

<section class="trust dark-field" id="controls" aria-labelledby="trust-title">
  <div class="trust-inner">
    <header class="trust-intro">
      <div>
        <p>Your brand. Your call.</p>
        <h2 id="trust-title">More content. Still unmistakably you.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Austi is being designed to keep your brand context, campaign drafts and feedback together. You decide what is ready to go out.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="control-boundary">
      <ol class="boundary-rules" aria-label="Brand and campaign controls">
        <li>
          <span><i aria-hidden="true"></i>01 · Brand context</span>
          <h3>Sound like you.</h3>
          <p>Start with your own website, product details and writing examples. Keep your voice and audience at the center of every brief.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span><i aria-hidden="true"></i>02 · One campaign</span>
          <h3>Connect the work.</h3>
          <p>Give your launch one clear idea, then adapt it to each channel. Keep the offer consistent while the format changes.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span><i aria-hidden="true"></i>03 · Your approval</span>
          <h3>Keep the final say.</h3>
          <p>Review the message, check product claims and make your edits before using a draft. Publishing and paid spend stay under your control.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <aside class="approval-example" aria-labelledby="approval-example-title">
        <p class="approval-example-kicker">Illustrative campaign · Sunday Supply</p>
        <h3 id="approval-example-title">The weekend edit.</h3>
        <p>One new collection. An ad, a social post and a launch email, all built around slower mornings and everyday essentials.</p>
        <footer>
          <span>Drafts ready for review</span>
          <strong>Review. Edit. Approve.</strong>
        </footer>
      </aside>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
